Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:45:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 052/107] render: particle systems run their child systems
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`children` was parsed and nothing read it. Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485:

- Each child entry is a template of its own system (parser 0x1401fe52a; keys and defaults GH
  0x1401eec40: the file is `name`, type static, probability 1, maxcount 10). Types (0x1401feff4):
  static 1, eventfollow 2, eventspawn 3, eventdeath 4. Children share the object's instance
  overrides (GH 0x140251f70 patches them from the same table).
- static: one instance, always on.
- eventfollow / eventspawn: for every spawned particle, each such child under its maxcount rolls
  its probability and takes an instance, a reused one reset (GH 0x140254f50) and prewarmed
  (GH 0x14025cfe0). A follow child moves with its particle every step; when the particle dies, its
  emitters stop (GH 0x140254ed0) and it lives out its particles.
- eventdeath: the same per dead particle, where it died (GH 0x14025c2e0).
- An instance's transform is translate (its particle) × the child's origin, angles and scale
  (GH 0x1402507e0). Here a child simulates in its parent's space: its particles spawn at that
  offset, turned and scaled by it, and stay where they were emitted.
- An event instance goes back to the pool when it has no particles and no emitter that can still
  emit (GH 0x1402524c0; inferred). A hidden parent clears its children's instances too.
- Inferred: a child with a controlpointstartindex takes its parent's control points from there on
  for those it doesn't define; children draw after their parent.

Event instances only simulate: one renderer per child entry draws them all in one pass (sprites)
or one instance at a time (ropes), so 350 rain splashes don't compile 350 shader passes.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B11 (P2)
